**FREE
//=======================================================================
// JUCUTLP - /include copy member: prototypes for JUCUTL's exported
// procedures (Part 7, lesson 07-01).
//
// JUCUTL is a business nickname only (docs/appendix/e-naming.md /
// part07-design-v1.md section 0.2 naming table): this member is used
// only within 07-01, so it follows style-guide.md's type+part+lesson+
// sequence naming, not the "persistent feature name" register. The
// object it describes lives in module M0701B (src/qrpglesrc/jucutl.rpgle),
// a NOMAIN utility module. This copy member's own real IBM i member
// name is JUCUTLP (10 characters or fewer; the .rpgleinc file name
// matches the member name exactly here, unlike jucutl.rpgle, whose
// file name differs from its real object name M0701B - see the header
// comment in that file).
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (self-include pattern for a NOMAIN module):
// ilerpgref75.txt's own /COPY-or-/INCLUDE section states this as a
// documented Tip (lines 7818-7822): "To facilitate application
// maintenance, you may want to place the prototypes of exported
// procedures in a separate source member. If you do, be sure to place
// a /COPY or /INCLUDE directive for that member in both the module
// containing the exported procedure and any modules that contain calls
// to the exported procedure." This file is exactly that separate
// member, included by BOTH jucutl.rpgle (the module that implements
// calcTaxTotal/sendMsg) and m0701s.rpgle (the module that calls them).
//
// IS THIS SELF-INCLUDE REQUIRED BY THE COMPILER, OR ONLY RECOMMENDED?
// Checked against the primary source, not guessed: it is RECOMMENDED,
// not compiler-enforced. ilerpgref75.txt line 38280-
// 38281 states "If the prototype is not specified, the prototype is
// implicitly defined using the information in the procedure interface"
// - so jucutl.rpgle's own dcl-proc calcTaxTotal/sendMsg would still
// compile and export fine even without including this file itself.
// What the self-include buys you, and what IS compiler-enforced once
// you choose to add it: ilerpgref75.txt lines 8388-8391 and 38289-38291
// both state "The procedure interface must match the corresponding
// prototype" - so once jucutl.rpgle also /includes this file, the
// compiler cross-checks calcTaxTotal's and sendMsg's actual dcl-pi
// against this member's dcl-pr and flags any drift at compile time,
// instead of only the caller-side (m0701s.rpgle) ever noticing a
// mismatch. That cross-check is the actual benefit, not a hard
// requirement to compile a NOMAIN module at all.
//
// /INCLUDE syntax used by both callers (bare member name - no file or
// library qualifier): per ilerpgref75.txt lines 7785-7793, "If a file
// name is not specified, QRPGLESRC is assumed" and "If a library is
// not specified, the library list is searched" - this matches style-
// guide.md's rule of never hardcoding library names in source. Both
// this member and jucutl.rpgle/m0701s.rpgle live in the same QRPGLESRC
// source file (per this repo's existing convention of one member per
// checked-in .rpgle/.rpgleinc file, see verify/lib/batch.mjs's
// CPYFRMSTMF-to-member transfer step), so no SRCFIL qualifier is coded
// here either:
//   /INCLUDE jucutlp
//
// **FREE on this file's own first line: ilerpgref75.txt lines 23295-
// 23298 state "Copy files are assumed to have column-limited source
// mode unless **FREE appears in the first line of the file. When the
// copy file ends, the source mode returns to the mode of the source
// file containing the /COPY or /INCLUDE directive" - so this **FREE is
// required for THIS member to itself be parsed as free-form (matching
// every other source file in this repo), independent of whichever mode
// the includer happens to use (both m0701s.rpgle and jucutl.rpgle are
// **FREE too, so in practice there is no mode mismatch either way, but
// the **FREE line here is not redundant - it is what makes this member
// self-consistent if it were ever /included from a fixed-form source).
//
// STATUS: hardware-UNTESTED (Part 7 draft; Part 6, which this module's
// logic is ported from, is itself not yet hardware-verified - SSH to
// PUB400 is rate-limited as of 2026-09-26). Nothing here has been
// compiled on PUB400 yet.
//
// Verified against work/design/refs/ilerpgref75.txt (IBM i 7.5 ILE RPG
// Language Reference, 73451 lines):
//   /COPY or /INCLUDE syntax, bare member name          lines 7773-7822
//     ("membername" format, QRPGLESRC/library-list
//     defaults), and the "separate source member for
//     exported-procedure prototypes" Tip
//   Copy-file source mode / **FREE interaction          lines 23282-23298
//   DCL-PR free-form prototype syntax (no EXTPGM/        lines 29340-29368
//     EXTPROC = prototype for a bound procedure call,
//     not a program call)
//   "procedure interface must match the corresponding    lines 8388-8391,
//     prototype" (why the self-include's cross-check      38289-38291,
//     works)                                               16927-16958
//   Bound-call default entry point = prototype name       lines 48121-48124
//     in upper case, when EXTPROC is not specified
//=======================================================================

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------
// calcTaxTotal - tax-inclusive total. Faithful port of F0605A's
// subprocedure of the same name (src/qrpglesrc/f0605s.rpgle lines 211-
// 228), itself a port of R0402A's C-spec logic (04-02, Z-ADD1580 /
// Z-ADD1.10 / MULT). 1580 x 1.10 = 1738.00 (04-02, hardware-verified
// 2026-09-25). No EXTPGM/EXTPROC keyword: this is a prototype for a
// bound call to a procedure in another module (M0701B), not a call to
// a separate *PGM object - contrast with F0605A's own r0409a prototype,
// which uses EXTPGM('R0409A') because R0409A really is a separate
// external program.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------
dcl-pr calcTaxTotal packed(9:2);
  amount packed(7:2) value;
  rate   packed(3:2) const options(*nopass);
end-pr;

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------
// sendMsg - the QCMDEXC/SNDPGMMSG-based observation channel from
// Part 6 (used because DSPLY defaults to QSYSOPR for a batch job -
// see jucutl.rpgle for the faithful port of the body). Same signature
// as F0605A's sendMsg (src/qrpglesrc/f0605s.rpgle lines 238-257): one
// CONST char(60) parameter, no return value.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------
dcl-pr sendMsg;
  text char(60) const;
end-pr;
